Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:10.230 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  hi everyone it's joanna here this eight  minutes morning workout will help you to  burn fat lose weight building muscles  and make you look good this workout was  created by personal trainer and  best-selling author jorge cruz and he  has helped over 3 million people with  this workout so if you want to lose  weight and you don't have the time for  it do this this workout is based on the  foundation of strength training i've  always emphasized the importance of  strength training and that it should be  part of your workout every one pound of  lean muscles you build in your body will  help you to burn an additional 30  calories at rest therefore the more lean  muscles you have the more calories your  body will be burning at rest which will  prompt weight loss in order for this  workout to work all i'm asking you to do  is to get up 10 minutes earlier in the  morning and do the workout it will  kickstart your metabolic rate you will  start burning fat it will give you the  energy you need and it will make you  feel good throughout the day there will  only be two exercises in a day do one  set of 12 repetition from exercise a  then immediately one set of 12  repetitions from exercise b  repeat the entire cycle three more times  without resting and then you are done so  let me show you the workouts  start your workout with a brief warm-up  by jogging on the spot for one minute or  jumping jacks  on monday the muscles we want to be  focusing on are our chest and our back  muscles for our chest let's do dumbbell  press lie on the mat on your back with  your knees bent and your feet flat on  the floor holding one dumbbell in each  hand bring your elbows in line with your  shoulders and make sure that your  dumbbells are in line with your chest  exhale as you slowly extend your arms  and press the dumbbells towards the  ceiling keep your elbows loose hold for  one second inhale as you return to the  starting point and repeat  as for your back the workout is dumbbell  row you can choose to sit on a chair  hold one dumbbell in each hand lean  slightly forward and keep your chest  open extend your arms straight down  exhale as you slowly bring your elbows  towards the ceiling and squeeze your  back muscles extend your arms right down  and repeat  alternatively you can choose to stand  and roll i prefer standing as you will  need to tighten your abs in order to  keep your back straight and your chest  open throughout the workout  on tuesdays we want to be working on our  shoulders and abs for shoulders the  workout is lateral raise stand with your  feet shoulder width apart keep your back  straight tighten your core  hold one dumbbell in each hand exhale as  you slowly lift the dumbbells just  slightly above your shoulders with your  palms facing the floor release slowly  and repeat the move  for abdominals we want to be working on  crunches lie on your back with your  knees bent cross your arms and just  place them between your chin and your  collarbone  as you exhale  slowly crunch up to a 45 degrees angle  inhale and lower yourself back down and  repeat the move  on wednesdays we want to be working on  our arms triceps and biceps  for triceps the workout is lying  kickback or head crunches  lie on your back with a dumbbell in each  hand  keep your arms straight but keep your  elbows loose during the workout the only  part that should be moving are your  forearms bend your elbows and lower the  dumbbells down close to your head exhale  and straighten your arms back up by  squeezing your triceps and repeat the  moves  [Music]  as for your biceps we want to be doing  bicep curls stand shoulder width apart  hold a dumbbell in each hand with your  palms facing up  exhale as you curl both arms up bringing  your palms towards your biceps keep your  elbows close to your sides throughout  the workout focus on moving only from  your elbow joints and not from your  shoulders inhale as you lower your arms  back down and repeat  and on thursdays we want to be working  on our thighs hamstrings and quads for  hamstrings the workout is leg lift you  will need a chair for this or a higher  platform  lie on your back and place your heels on  the chair exhale as you lift your bum  and your upper thighs off the floor and  squeeze the back part of your thighs  which are your hamstrings hold for one  second inhale as you lower your butt  down and repeat the move  as for your quads let's do my favorite  workout squats stand with your feet  slightly wider than shoulder width apart  keeping your back straight and chest  open throughout the workout lower your  body down into a squat position and do  not let your knees extend past your toes  push up with your heels and repeat the  move you should be feeling on your  thighs and your butt  [Music]  on fridays let's work on our calves and  butt  so let's start with calf raises stance  shoulder width apart and you can choose  to hold a dumbbell in each hand  keep your chest and your shoulders open  and your abs tight exhale as you lift  your heels off the floor and rise onto  your toes hold for one second  inhale as you slowly lower yourself back  down alternatively you can choose to do  this on a higher platform which will  give you a higher intensity as well  now let's move on to kickbacks for your  butt  kneel on all fours with your knees hip  width apart your hands slightly wider  than your shoulders and your fingers  pointing forward bring your right leg  into a 90 degree angle exhale as you  slowly push your foot towards the  ceiling  bring it back to a 90 degrees position  and repeat  so do 12 repetitions on one side and 12  repetitions on the other side  [Music]  and on saturdays the muscles we want to  focus on are our inner thighs and outer  thighs  let's start with inner thigh leg raise  lie on your left side with your left  elbow and forearm supporting your upper  body bend your right knee and keep your  right foot on the floor for extra  balance keep your left leg straight  exhale as you lift your left foot as  high as you can hold for one second feel  and squeeze your inner thighs  inhale and lower it back down for a more  advanced version you can choose to place  your right foot on your left leg do one  set on your left leg and then switch  side and do another 12 repetitions on  your right side  as for your outer thigh let's do the  peeing dog movement  kneel on all fours with your knees hip  width apart your hands slightly wider  than your shoulders and your fingers  pointing forward keep your back straight  and tighten your core throughout the  workout keep your leg bent at a 90  degree angles exhale as you raise your  leg out to the side hold for one second  and squeeze your outer thigh inhale as  you lower your leg back down to the  starting point and repeat  same thing do 12 reps for one side and  switch sides and your out with a quick  total body stretches and you are done  if you do not have dumbbells you can  always be creative and use household  items make two weights one heavier  weights and one lighter weights with the  heavier weights use two big milk butter  and you can fill them up with water or  fill them up with stones to make them  even heavier for the lighter weights  use  two small bottles same thing use water  to fill them up or to increase your  weight use stones  this workout is exclusively for weight  loss and not for fitness gain in terms  of cardio therefore i would encourage  you to spend at least two to three times  weekly to do your regular cardio or to  do some cardio exercises according to my  videos according to jorge cruz if you  were to do this workout and to eat clean  and healthy you will be looking at  losing an average of 2 pounds per week  so spend eight minutes in the morning do  this workout for the next four weeks and  see the results  for new fitness food and motivational  videos please like share and subscribe  to my youtube channel and website  do follow me on facebook instagram and  twitter to stay connected with me thanks  guys  [Music]  you

